If a patient cannot taper an opioid and continues a high-dosage-opioid then every clinician should monitor the patient and should mitigate an overdose-risk with an overdose-education and should offer a naloxone-dose.
If a patient cannot taper an opioid and continues a high-risk-opioid-regimen then every clinician should monitor the patient and should mitigate an overdose-risk with an overdose-education and should offer a naloxone-dose.
